# Half-Life satchel charge. Measured by vrcardgen, finished by hand.
#
# Part J: "Take one from the chest; throw it or set it down gently where you
# want it."
#
# NOTHING ON IT MOVES. The tool found no moving bones at all, which is the
# right answer: a satchel is a brick with a radio receiver. There is no pin,
# no spoon and no fuse - it waits for the detonator, which is a separate
# weapon with a card of its own.
#
# What this card says is that the satchel is RELEASED rather than fired.
# Throwing it and setting it down are the same gesture at different speeds,
# and both are the world's business (Part I) rather than the weapon's.

weapon v_satchel
match  bones 44  seqs 4  hash 0x04798c0b

# The bone every position in this card is measured in - the controls, the
# grab points, the chamber, the ejection port. Nothing recorded it until
# the engine had to place a control in the world to ask whether a thumb is
# near it; the simulator never needed one, because it never works in world
# space. Taken from the generator, which has always called this bone the
# WEAPON BODY and is what measured these numbers in the first place.
body   "psx_v_satchel"

type   thrown
fuse   0           # it waits for the radio
